        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kodi Smit-McPhee, Eric Bana, Franka Potente\n- Films: The Road, Let Me In, ParaNorman, Dawn of the Planet of the Apes, Romulus, My Father\n- Characters: The Boy, Owen, Norman Babcock, Alexander, Nightcrawler\n- Topics: film roles, film reception, box office, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- In 2007, the film adaptation \"Romulus, My Father\" was released starring Eric Bana, Franka Potente, and Kodi Smit-McPhee.\n- Kodi Smit-McPhee is best known for playing The Boy in \"The Road,\" Owen in \"Let Me In,\" Norman Babcock in \"ParaNorman,\" Alexander in \"Dawn of the Planet of the Apes,\" and Nightcrawler in a 2016 film.\n- \"ParaNorman\" mainly received positive reviews.\n- \"ParaNorman\" was a modest box office success, earning $107 million against a $60 million budget.",
